        "id": "ch11_2-1",
        "text": "Editing Text Files with nano\nIf you aren\u2019t using (or can\u2019t use) the GUI, you have numerous text editors availa-\nble to you. The most powerful of these are vi and emacs , which you\u2019ll hear many\npeople go on about. However, both these programs require a learning curve. For\nbeginners who want to just edit the file and move on, I recommend nano , which\noffers a friendly, menu-driven interface.\nTo open a file in nano , type nano  filename , such as nano file1 . The file opens in\nthe nano editor, as shown in Figure 11-1.\nYou can then edit or type in that file as much as you need to.\nCHAPTER 11 Putting the X in Text 205\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Saving your work as you go\n\u2022 Saving and moving on with your life\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
